abseil 20260107.1 install export fix (backport of the upstream master
change): heterogeneous_lookup_testing is missing its TESTONLY marker, so
it is installed into abslTargets.cmake while its link interface names
absl::test_instance_tracker (internal testonly, never installed) and
GTest::gmock (external). find_package(absl) on the installed prefix then
hard-fails loading the Config -- which is exactly what cpp-pkg's probe
does. Applied by cpp-pkg via `patches = [...]` on the absl dev-dependency.

--- a/absl/container/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/absl/container/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1119,6 +1119,7 @@
     absl::config
     absl::test_instance_tracker
     GTest::gmock
+  TESTONLY
 )
 
 absl_cc_library(
